A game machine shows a three-digit number. Its hundreds digit is 6, its tens digit is 1, and its units digit is \(X\).
The machine pays:
4 tokens if the number is divisible by 2 but not by 3;
8 tokens if it is divisible by 3 but not by 2;
12 tokens if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.
Noa played once and won 12 tokens. How many different values can \(X\) have?
